# Build-context exclusions for the repo-root images (api, worker, agent,
# railway-agent-worker, the two model sidecars).
#
# Every one of those Dockerfiles COPYs a handful of named paths, so anything
# here was being sent to the daemon and then ignored. The root context measured
# ~391 MB, most of it node_modules and .git.
#
# Nothing here is COPYed by any Dockerfile — check before adding a path that
# is, since the failure would be a missing file at build time rather than a
# slow build.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Environments and secrets. .env is gitignored, but a build context is not a
# git operation: without this line it would be sent to the daemon and could
# land in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
.venv
venv/

# Caches and build output
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The frontend is built from its own context (apps/frontend); the backend
# images have no use for it.
apps/frontend/

# Documentation, prototypes, and 6.6 MB of recorded evaluation runs. The
# services read none of them at runtime — the figures are baked into the
# frontend bundle at build time by scripts/sync_eval_artifacts.py.
docs/
design/
results/
*.md

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
